  "attested_inventories_note": "These two klt signoff --attest envelopes content-hash EVERY file their inventory lists, so the inventories -- not this registry's live_pins table -- are the authoritative lists; no per-file live_pins entry is added for them. An inventory-only file (tests/, the rtl/ benches and mutants, README.md, LICENSE, the three workflows) carries a weaker obligation than a live pin: it is an ordinary editable source, but the affected envelope must be re-attested in the same change. The audit in tests/test_byte_frozen_sources.py does NOT fire for them -- discover_recorded_sources() walks *.py outside tests/ only, so .sv, .yml, README.md, LICENSE and everything under tests/ are excluded by construction. Their freshness check is klt signoff --check, run by signoff.yml on every pull request and on every push to main, which exits 3 on drift. The 45 item 9 rows in live_pins are the subset the audit can discover, and they keep the stronger do-not-edit rule. Regenerating an envelope from an unchanged inventory leaves signoff/block-manifest.signoff.json byte-identical; changing an inventory also requires re-rendering that report and updating the content_hash signoff/block-manifest.json declares. Measured against d5ac9f6 under the klayout-tools pin in signoff/requirements.txt; see the doc for the probe table.",
  "audit": "tests/test_byte_frozen_sources.py",
